  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a rooted tree with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN); node 111 is the root. For each valid iii, the iii-th node has a value viv_ivi​ and another parameter mim_imi​.\n\nA leaf is a node without sons. Let's denote the number of leaf nodes in the tree by LLL and their numbers by l1,l2,…,lLl_1, l_2, \\ldots, l_Ll1​,l2​,…,lL​, in increasing order. Then, for each valid iii, let's define the answer for the leaf lil_ili​ in the following way:\n\n\nConsider the path from the root to lil_ili​. For each node on this path (including the root and this leaf), choose a non-negative integer and multiply the value of this node by it.\nSum up the resulting values of all nodes on this path.\nThe answer aia_iai​ for this leaf is defined as the maximum possible remainder of this sum modulo mlim_{l_i}mli​​.\nFind the answers for all leaves.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤81 \\le T \\le 81≤T≤8",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\le N \\le 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤x,y≤N1 \\le x, y \\le N1≤x,y≤N",
      "1≤vi≤10181 \\le v_i \\le 10^{18}1≤vi​≤1018 for each valid iii",
      "1≤mi≤10181 \\le m_i \\le 10^{18}1≤mi​≤1018 for each valid iii",
      "the graph described on the input is a tree",
      "Subtasks"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nEach of the following N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy denoting that nodes xxx and yyy are connected by an edge.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers v1,v2,…,vNv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_Nv1​,v2​,…,vN​.\nThe last line contains NNN space-separated integers m1,m2,…,mNm_1, m_2, \\ldots, m_Nm1​,m2​,…,mN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing LLL space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aLa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_La1​,a2​,…,aL​.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n5\n1 2\n2 5\n1 3\n3 4\n2 3 4 6 7\n1 2 3 2 10",
        "output": "0 9",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: There are only two leaves, l1=4l_1 = 4l1​=4 and l2=5l_2 = 5l2​=5. The answers for them are a1=0a_1 = 0a1​=0 and a2=9a_2 = 9a2​=9."
      }
    ]
  },
